      "content": "These groups often cite misinterpretations of early racial science, such as discredited theories of biological determinism, to claim inherent, fixed differences between races. They frequently reference skewed historical narratives, suggesting a supposed \"golden age\" of white dominance that they claim is currently being undermined. Furthermore, they often leverage heavily selective or distorted historical data, framing demographic changes as deliberate invasions rather than complex social phenomena. These pseudo-scientific and historically manipulative arguments form the bedrock of their self-justification for racial hierarchy.",
      "source": "target",
