      "content": "These arguments often operationalize \"culture\" as being inextricably and immutably tied to specific, predominantly white European ancestry. They posit that \"Western civilization\" operates on a set of unique, ethnically defined cultural capital that cannot be shared or sustained by groups they deem fundamentally different or incompatible. The threat of \"replacement\" is framed not just demographically, but as a qualitative erosion of the civilization's core character. This linkage reframes racial difference as a fundamental, existential incompatibility between groups, allowing them to bypass overt slurs by claiming to advocate for \"cultural purity\" or \"heritage defense.\"",
      "source": "target",
